        {
            "name": "Book notes: Atomic Habits",
            "document_markdown": "# Atomic Habits - Key Takeaways\n\n## The 4 Laws of Behavior Change\n\n### 1. Make it Obvious\n- Use implementation intentions: \"I will [behavior] at [time] in [location]\"\n- Use habit stacking: \"After [current habit], I will [new habit]\"\n- Design your environment for success\n\n### 2. Make it Attractive\n- Use temptation bundling\n- Join a culture where your desired behavior is normal\n- Create a motivation ritual\n\n### 3. Make it Easy\n- Reduce friction for good habits\n- Use the Two-Minute Rule\n- Automate your habits when possible\n\n### 4. Make it Satisfying\n- Use reinforcement: reward yourself immediately\n- Use a habit tracker\n- Never miss twice\n\n## Favorite Quotes\n> \"You do not rise to the level of your goals. You fall to the level of your systems.\"\n\n> \"Every action you take is a vote for the type of person you wish to become.\"\n",
            "updated_at": 1775160259203,
            "split_top_ratio": 0.39317156616865484,
            "linked_record_ids": [
                2919,
                2940
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "Weekly planning template",
            "document_markdown": "## This Week's Focus Areas\n\n1. Complete the Spanish B1 module 5\n2. Read 3 chapters of \"Deep Work\"\n3. Finish the home office setup\n4. Schedule dentist appointment\n5. Meal prep for the week\n\n## Reflection\n- What went well last week?\n- What could be improved?\n- What am I grateful for?\n",
            "updated_at": 1775137555325,
            "split_top_ratio": 0.55,
            "linked_record_ids": []
        },
        {
            "name": "Morning routine checklist",
            "document_markdown": "## My Ideal Morning (5:30 AM - 8:00 AM)\n\n### Wake up & Hydrate (5:30)\n- Glass of water with lemon\n- 5 minutes of deep breathing\n\n### Move (5:45)\n- 20 min stretching or yoga\n- Cold shower\n\n### Mind (6:15)\n- 15 min meditation\n- 10 min journaling\n\n### Learn (6:45)\n- 15 min Spanish lesson\n- 15 min reading\n\n### Plan (7:15)\n- Review today's tasks\n- Set top 3 priorities\n- Check calendar\n\n### Fuel (7:30)\n- Healthy breakfast\n- Vitamins & supplements",
            "updated_at": 1775124039600,
            "split_top_ratio": 0.55,
            "linked_record_ids": []
        },
        {
            "name": "Stoic philosophy notes",
            "document_markdown": "# Key Stoic Principles\n\n## Dichotomy of Control\nFocus only on what you can control: your thoughts, actions, and responses.\nLet go of what you cannot: other people's opinions, the weather, the past.\n\n## Memento Mori\nRemember that life is finite. This isn't morbid - it's motivating.\nUse it to prioritize what truly matters.\n\n## Amor Fati\nLove your fate. Everything that happens is an opportunity to practice virtue.\n\n## Favorite Quotes\n> \"The happiness of your life depends upon the quality of your thoughts.\" - Marcus Aurelius\n\n> \"We suffer more in imagination than in reality.\" - Seneca\n\n> \"It's not what happens to you, but how you react to it that matters.\" - Epictetus\n\n## Books to Read\n- Meditations by Marcus Aurelius\n- Letters from a Stoic by Seneca\n- Discourses by Epictetus\n- The Daily Stoic by Ryan Holiday",
            "updated_at": 1775121474613,
            "split_top_ratio": 0.55,
            "linked_record_ids": []
        }
    ],
